## Skills and Automations

Repository-local assistant assets are under `.agents/`:

### Skills (`.agents/skills/`)

- `apr-demo-run`: run and control the standard local demo sequence.
- `apr-pipeline-audit`: audit Bronze/Silver/Gold artifacts and data quality.
- `apr-dashboard-review`: verify dashboard behavior and API-connected demo readiness.
- `apr-twin-evaluation`: evaluate scenario outcomes vs twin rules and thresholds.

### Automation Prompt Templates (`.agents/automations/`)

- `daily-health-check.md`: daily local health/status prompt template.
- `repo-briefing.md`: periodic implementation and readiness briefing template.
- `weekly-twin-audit.md`: weekly scenario-based twin behavior audit template.

These templates are intentionally architecture-safe and scoped to the current local MVP.

## Operations Quick Commands

Run end-to-end local batch:

```powershell
python scripts/run_mvp.py --days 7 --freq-minutes 5 --apr-id APR-001
```

Manual pipeline:

```powershell
python -m apr_twin.synthetic.generator --days 7 --freq-minutes 5 --apr-id APR-001
python -m apr_twin.pipelines.bronze_to_silver
python -m apr_twin.pipelines.silver_to_gold
```

API health checks:

```powershell
Invoke-RestMethod http://127.0.0.1:8000/health
Invoke-RestMethod "http://127.0.0.1:8000/twin/state?apr_id=APR-001"
```

Tests:

```powershell
python -m pytest -q
```

Optional data override:

```powershell
$env:APR_DATA_DIR = "C:\temp\apr-data"
```
